course: ukrainian-street
lesson: 8
title: Counting on: nine to eighty
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Ukrainian numbers after ten are built like Lego: -NAdtsyat works like English «-teen», so odyNAdtsyat is eleven and p'yatNAdtsyat is fifteen.
explain: The tens end in -dtsyat or -desyat, like English «-ty»: DVAdtsyat is twenty, p'yatdesYAt is fifty.
explain: The big trap is the same as «fifteen» and «fifty» in English: p'yatNAdtsyat (15) and p'yatdesYAt (50) sound close, so listen for -NAdtsyat or -desYAt.
explain: And there is one odd one out: forty is not «four-ty» but a word all of its own, SOrok — so when the seeker in hide-and-seek counts to forty, listen for SOrok.
fact: DEvyat means nine, with the stress on the first syllable.
fact: DEsyat means ten; «do desyaty», up to ten, is how far the seeker counts in a quick hide-and-seek.
fact: DEvyat (9) and DEsyat (10) differ by one sound, v or s.
fact: odyNAdtsyat means eleven, and the ending -nadtsyat works like English «-teen».
fact: dvaNAdtsyat means twelve.
fact: p'yatNAdtsyat means fifteen, a common number to count to in hide-and-seek.
fact: DVAdtsyat means twenty, heard in counting, prices and scores.
fact: TRYdtsyat means thirty.
fact: SOrok means forty; it is the odd one, not built from the word for four.
fact: p'yatdesYAt means fifty, with the stress at the end, and it is easy to confuse with p'yatNAdtsyat, fifteen.
fact: shistdesYAt means sixty, also stressed at the end.
fact: sImdesyat means seventy and vIsimdesyat means eighty, both stressed at the start.
exercise: What does DEvyat mean? | Nine | Ten | Ninety | Nineteen
exercise: What does DEsyat mean? | Ten | Nine | Twelve | Death
exercise: Which sound tells DEvyat (9) from DEsyat (10)? | v or s | d or t | the last letter t | nothing, they are the same
exercise: What does odyNAdtsyat mean? | Eleven | One hundred | Ten | Twenty-one
exercise: What English ending works like -NAdtsyat? | «-teen» | «-ty» | «-th» | «-hundred»
exercise: What does dvaNAdtsyat mean? | Twelve | Twenty | Two | Twenty-two
exercise: What does p'yatNAdtsyat mean? | Fifteen | Fifty | Five | Fifty-five
exercise: What does DVAdtsyat mean? | Twenty | Twelve | Two hundred | Thirty
exercise: What does TRYdtsyat mean? | Thirty | Thirteen | Three | Twenty
exercise: What is forty in Ukrainian? | SOrok | chotyRYdesyat | chotyrNAdtsyat | sImdesyat
exercise: Why is SOrok the odd one out? | It is not built from the word for four | It means fourteen | It has no stress | It is borrowed from English
exercise: What does p'yatdesYAt mean? | Fifty | Fifteen | Five | Five hundred
exercise: Where is the stress in p'yatdesYAt? | At the end, YAT | At the start, P'YAT | In the middle, DE | Nowhere
exercise: What does shistdesYAt mean? | Sixty | Sixteen | Six | Seventy
exercise: What does sImdesyat mean? | Seventy | Seventeen | Seven | Eighty
exercise: What does vIsimdesyat mean? | Eighty | Eighteen | Eight | Seventy
test: «p'yatNAdtsyat, p'yatdesYAt, both fifty right» Which is right? | No: p'yatNAdtsyat is 15, p'yatdesYAt is 50 | Yes, both are fifty | Both are fifteen | p'yatNAdtsyat is 5, p'yatdesYAt is 50
test: «forty must be chotyRYdesyat, like four + ty» Which is right? | No, forty is its own word, SOrok | Yes, chotyRYdesyat is forty | Forty is chotyrNAdtsyat | Forty is TRYdtsyat
test: The seeker counts «… vIsim, DEvyat, DEsyat — ya shukAyu!». How far did he count? | To ten | To nine | To eighty | To ninety
test: A kid says he scored DVAdtsyat goals this year. How many? | Twenty | Twelve | Two | Two hundred
test: At the market a man says «sImdesyat». Your friend hears «seventeen». What did the man say? | Seventy | Seventeen | Seven | Seven hundred
test: What would happen if you heard «DEvyat» as «DEsyat» in hide-and-seek? | You'd think he counted to ten when he was at nine | Nothing, they mean the same | You'd think he counted to ninety | You'd think he said hello
test: dvaNAdtsyat kids, and DEsyat go home. How many stay? | dva | DEsyat | odYn | try
test: TRYdtsyat plus DEsyat makes… | SOrok | p'yatdesYAt | DVAdtsyat | TRYdtsyat
test: In a game the shop sign says vIsimdesyat coins, and the cartoon character pays eighteen. What went wrong? | vIsimdesyat is eighty, not eighteen | Nothing, it is eighteen | It is eight | It is eight hundred
test: «shut up, sixty is shistNAdtsyat» Which is right? | No, sixty is shistdesYAt; -NAdtsyat would make sixteen | Yes, that's sixty | Sixty is SOrok | Sixty is sImdesyat
test: Which number is NOT built from its small number plus a ten-ending? | SOrok | TRYdtsyat | p'yatdesYAt | sImdesyat
exam: State the numeral signified by p'yatNAdtsyat, being careful to distinguish it from a numeral of similar sound. | Fifteen | Fifty | Five | Fifty-five
exam: Identify the numeral which, alone among the tens here considered, is not formed from the corresponding unit. | SOrok, forty | TRYdtsyat, thirty | shistdesYAt, sixty | vIsimdesyat, eighty
exam: Select the response consistent with the established function of the element -NAdtsyat. | It corresponds to the English termination «-teen» | It corresponds to the English termination «-ty» | It denotes the hundreds | It denotes ordinal position
exam: Ascertain the aggregate of DVAdtsyat and TRYdtsyat. | Fifty, p'yatdesYAt | Forty, SOrok | Thirty-two | Fifteen, p'yatNAdtsyat
